  abstract = {We applied double-flap reconstruction with a vascularized fibula osteo flap and a Y-shaped anterolateral thigh (ALT) flap, which was separated into a fascial flap and a de-epithelialized fat flap to replace the temporomandibular joint capsule and temporal soft tissue volume, respectively. A 16-year-old girl had a rapidly growing mandibular osteosarcoma. A left fibula osteo flap and left ALT flap were prepared in a prefabricated manner using a three-dimensional model and a prebent titanium plate. The de-epithelialized fat flap was used to prevent the depression deformation at the temporal area, and the fascial flap was used to cover around the alternate condylar head made by the fibula. The peroneal artery and veins were microscopically anastomosed to the distal end of the artery and veins of the descending branch of the ALT flap in a flow-through manner. At 12 months after surgery, the occlusal function and aesthetic balance were excellent.},
